In the late afternoon I walked back into the old town.
I walked across a large square.
Everywhere people enjoyed the good weather.
There I saw a very busy café.
I went inside and ordered a piece of cake.
The waiter said: "That is six euros, please."
I paid and went back outside.
There I sat down at a small table.
The cake tasted really very good.
Then I took the mobile phone out of the rucksack.
I took a few photos for you, Sofia.
I just sent them to you!
After that I stayed there for a long time.
I simply listened to the people around me.
They talked and laughed a lot.
It turned into a perfect afternoon.
